 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "AVOID with a mob action (DEFEAT_ENTITY or LOOK_AT_ENTITY) fails ObtainabilityTest.everyGoalTargetIsARealVanillaId: the entity id of the action is looked up as an item. AVOID is limited to block and item actions (eat, break, place).",
  "PlaytestTest cannot drive EQUIP on a slot tag (#minecraft:head_armor, chest_armor): the step \"did not advance\". A concrete piece (철 투구) works.",
  "A taught word can rename another object of the sentence: a SEQUENCE step that taught 엔더맨 printed the ender pearl as 엔더맨 (엔더맨을 물리친 후에 엔더맨을 구하세요). Teach the object of the last part to avoid it.",
  "A sequence repeats the object of both parts in full (다이아몬드 투구를 만든 후에 다이아몬드 투구를 쓰세요); a pronoun or an omitted object would read better.",
  "Counts above 20 are printed as digits plus a counter (24장, 22개) instead of a native or Sino-Korean number; the batch kept every count at 20 or below.",
  "ACQUIRE_ITEM prints 만드세요 for craftable items (하얀색 현수막, 끈) although any acquisition counts, and a CRAFT goal on the same item is a duplicate signature.",
  "REACH_HEIGHT inside HOLD_WHILE prints \"높이 40 이하로 내려가세요\" in the clue and 아래로 내려가요 in the hint (digits in the clue).",
  "unknownOverOneShare counts every multi-word vanilla name as one unknown word, so a sentence with two new item names (철 문 옆에 돌 버튼을) is over the limit; the lesson is to anchor on a known word (문, 제작대) or to space the new words.",
  "The duplicate-signature and verb-object-pair ratchets use the whole path: many natural steps (CRAFT paper, PLACE chest or barrel, DEFEAT enderman) are already taken, so a batch needs conditions (TIME, SKY, HOLDING, NEAR_BLOCK) or other objects to stay unique.",
  "A TRADE count is checked against what the villager pays (selling) or hands over (buying), not what the clue says; the vanilla amounts per offer (24 paper, 20 wheat, 15 beetroot) can exceed the clue count."
 ]
}
